From 78702b5e5878fee8ceba227ce62cbe7803a0f13d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tryinget <markus@team-wangler.de>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 02:53:17 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 11/13] feat(frame): diagnose shadow-hosted, name-matched and
 out-of-process iframes

Dogfooding frame.diagnose on real pages showed three blind spots:

- The DOM inventory used document.querySelectorAll("iframe"), which
  never sees frames rendered inside a custom element's shadow tree; on
  MDN it reported 0 iframes against 6 extension frames and blamed
  "nested or detached frames". Walk open shadow roots and report the
  host path as shadowHost.
- srcdoc and about:blank iframes were never correlated with the CDP
  tree although CDP names a frame after the iframe's name or id. Match
  on that, and warn only about blank frames that still have no handle.
- Out-of-process iframes (YouTube embeds, cross-site widgets) are absent
  from Page.getFrameTree on the tab's own target, so frame.js cannot
  reach them; the report showed "cdp -" without saying so. Add a
  warning that names the working alternative (frame.switch, page.read
  and click by ref when the content script answers).

The count-mismatch warning now states how many frames are nested and
how many sit in shadow roots, and the text renderer abbreviates
kilobyte-long embed runner URLs (--json keeps them). The real-Chrome
e2e fixture gains a shadow-hosted iframe and asserts the id-based
srcdoc match.

